SWEET WLAN run F1 (patch 0134, docs/research/53-wd4-msgbuf-ring-plan.md s5.2 and s7 step 2), boot-arg sweetwlan=8 = run E (patch 0133, levels 1-7 unchanged: same log, same reads and stores) + READ-ONLY dumps of the running firmware, after W17 found the shared structure and BEFORE the CA7 re-halt (PCIe core registers after it). No new store class and no new mapping.
F1 dumps: the whole shared structure (35 words, pciedev_shared_t v7), the two mailbox data words, ring_info (19 words) and the 5 ring_mem entries it points to, the console (buffer, size, write index; the last 4 KiB before the index, at most 128 lines printed), the PCIe core registers 0xC10/0xC14/0xC18 (+ 0xC30/0xC34, SRPWR), the ELBI IRQ0..2 status and enables, the EP Command. Every pointer the firmware hands over passes swl_f1_span_ok() (aligned, in the RAM, in the BAR2 window W17 selected) before a word is read; one that fails is reported and skipped. Stops (CA7 re-halted by the unchanged restore): flags ASSERT/TRAP before or after the dumps, a block of 2+ words that is all ones, any RC interrupt enable, a failed precondition (re-checked before the console and the last flags read), a bus error. A console write index beyond the buffer is refused as DHD does. The PCIe core group (all-ones register, mailbox mask not 0 = stops) runs AFTER the re-halt (review 0134 F1); its two window selects are the only stores (existing tuples).
NOT done (needs a new mapping, i.e. a new guard class; open question for the driver): the S2MPU HSI2 dump (0x14480000) and the RC DBI Command register: sw_map() maps no such page.
Glue: level 8 accepted and named "F1". HW-WRITE path: unreviewed.

